CAT = "ssvLaw"; SEG = "LAW"
Q = [
("Which body administers Ontario's Liquor Licence and Control Act, 2019?",
 'The AGCO', ['The LCBO', 'The Ministry of Health', 'The local police service'],
 'The Alcohol and Gaming Commission of Ontario (AGCO) administers the LLCA and licenses and inspects licensed premises. The LCBO sells and distributes liquor; it does not license bars.'),
('Who sets the standards and requirements that licensees must meet in addition to the Act and regulations?',
 'The AGCO Registrar', ['The local fire chief', 'Each municipality', 'The LCBO board'],
 "The LLCA lets the Registrar set standards, published as the Registrar's Interim Standards and Requirements for Liquor, on top of the Act and its regulations."),
('A bar hires a new server. When must the server hold a valid certificate from an AGCO Board-approved training course?',
 'Before working with liquor', ['Within 30 days of hiring', 'Before the first inspection', 'After a probation period'],
 'Everyone involved in the sale, service, sampling or delivery of liquor must hold a valid certificate from a Board-approved course before working, not after a grace period.'),
('Which worker at a licensed restaurant must hold a valid server training certificate?',
 'A host who takes drink orders', ['A dishwasher in the kitchen', 'A cook who never handles liquor', 'An office bookkeeper'],
 'The training rule covers every person involved in the sale, service, sampling or delivery of liquor, or in taking orders for its sale. Taking drink orders is enough.'),
('Which security staff must hold a certificate from an AGCO Board-approved course?',
 'Security the licensee employs', ['Police officers on paid duty', 'Valet parking attendants', 'Coat check staff at the door'],
 'The Interim Standards require certification for security staff the licensee employs (or, at a stadium, uses). The AGCO also calls it best practice for contracted security.'),
('At a golf course with a Golf Course Endorsement, which staff must hold an approved training certificate?',
 'Cart staff and course marshals', ['Pro shop cashiers', 'Groundskeepers on mowers', 'Golf lesson instructors'],
 'Staff selling and serving liquor from motorized vending carts and course marshals at Golf Course Endorsement holders must hold an approved certificate.'),
('A worker holds only a retail-only liquor training certificate. Where may that worker sell or serve liquor?',
 'Only in a licensed retail store', ['In any licensed bar or pub', 'At catered weddings only', 'On golf course drink carts'],
 'The AGCO approves retail-only programs for licensed retail stores. A worker with only that certificate cannot sell or serve outside a retail store.'),
('An AGCO inspector asks a bar manager to show proof that a server is certified. When may an inspector ask for this?',
 'At any time', ['After a complaint', 'Once a year', 'With a warrant'],
 "AGCO inspectors may ask a licensee for proof of a staff member's certification at any time, so licensees are encouraged to keep copies."),
('Why are licensees encouraged to keep copies of staff training certificates on file?',
 'To show proof to inspectors', ['To claim a training tax credit', 'To renew the liquor licence', 'To share with other bars'],
 'Inspectors may ask for proof of certification at any time. Keeping copies on file makes the proof quick to show.'),
('When may an AGCO inspector inspect a licensed premises?',
 'At any reasonable time', ['During business hours', "With 24 hours' notice", 'After a police report'],
 'AGCO inspections can happen at any reasonable time, as a routine check or because of a complaint or police report.'),
('During an AGCO inspection, what should staff do if the inspector wants to take photos or samples?',
 'Allow it', ['Ask for a warrant first', 'Wait for the owner to arrive', 'Refuse until closing time'],
 'Staff should cooperate fully: let the inspector walk through the premises, take photos or samples, or seize items, and never obstruct the inspection.'),
('Where must a liquor sales licence be displayed?',
 'Somewhere easily seen inside', ["In the manager's locked office", 'On the outside door only', 'In the staff room'],
 'The licence and any endorsements must be posted in a conspicuous place in the licensed premises, where customers, inspectors and police can see it.'),
("A bar's licence is suspended for ten days. What must the licensee post?",
 "The Registrar's suspension sign", ['A closed for renovations sign', "A copy of the inspector's report", 'Nothing, if it stays closed'],
 'A suspended licensee must post the sign the Registrar provides, visible from outside the premises, for the whole suspension.'),
('Which of these is a common licence violation found during AGCO inspections?',
 'Going over licensed capacity', ['Playing music too loudly', 'Changing the menu often', 'Hiring a new cook'],
 'Common violations include permitting intoxication, serving outside hours, disorderly conduct, exceeding the capacity on the licence and serving people under 19.'),
('A licensee receives a Notice of Proposal to suspend the licence. Who hears an appeal?',
 'The Licence Appeal Tribunal', ["The LCBO's head office", 'Ontario Small Claims Court', 'The municipal council'],
 'A licensee may request a hearing before the Licence Appeal Tribunal (LAT), which is part of Tribunals Ontario and independent of the AGCO.'),
('After a Notice of Proposal to revoke a licence, how long does the licensee have to request a hearing?',
 '15 days', ['5 days', '30 days', '60 days'],
 'The licensee has 15 days to request a hearing before the Licence Appeal Tribunal. Without a request, the Registrar may carry out the proposal.'),
("Which outcome can follow a violation of the LLCA, its regulations or the Registrar's standards?",
 'A monetary penalty', ['A free warning only', 'A higher drink price', 'A new liquor licence'],
 'Violations can lead to warnings, monetary penalties, or a notice of proposal to suspend or revoke the licence.'),
("Under the AGCO's risk-based licensing, why might a bar's licence carry extra conditions?",
 'Past incidents at the bar', ['A change in menu prices', 'Hiring a new head chef', 'Higher sales than last year'],
 'The AGCO may place conditions on a licence because of incidents or non-compliance at the premises, or proactively to prevent specific issues.'),
("A bar's licence includes conditions. Who on staff should know about them?",
 'Managers, servers and security', ['Just the owner', 'The head bartender', 'Managers, not servers'],
 'The AGCO tells licensees to make sure all staff, including management, servers and security, know any licence conditions and follow them.'),
('Which section of the LLCA says no person shall sell liquor to anyone who is or appears to be intoxicated?',
 'Section 32', ['Section 52', 'Section 24', 'Section 43'],
 'LLCA section 32 bars selling or supplying liquor to anyone who is or appears to be intoxicated. Section 52 sets out civil liability; sections 24 and 43 are in Regulation 746/21.'),
('Under Regulation 746/21, a licensee must not permit which practice?',
 'Encouraging heavy drinking', ['Selling food after midnight', 'Serving non-alcoholic drinks', 'Posting a drink menu'],
 "Section 24 of Regulation 746/21 says the licensee shall not engage in or permit practices that may tend to encourage patrons' immoderate consumption of liquor."),
('Under section 43(1) of Regulation 746/21, a licensee must not permit intoxication, unlawful gambling or disorderly conduct where?',
 'Premises and adjacent areas', ['The bar counter alone', 'Indoors, not on patios', 'Inside the front door'],
 "The duty covers the licensed premises and adjacent areas under the licensee's exclusive control, not just the room where drinks are served."),
('A patron who was served while visibly intoxicated crashes and injures another driver. What does LLCA section 52 allow?',
 'A claim against the seller', ['A claim against the AGCO', 'A claim against the LCBO', 'No claim at all'],
 "Section 52 lets a person injured by someone sold liquor while apparently intoxicated recover compensation from the seller, and covers the seller's employees and agents."),
('Section 52 applies when liquor is sold to a person whose condition means more drinking would:',
 'Make them a danger to others', ['Make them stay much longer', 'Raise the size of their bill', 'Make them a little sleepy'],
 'Section 52 applies where drinking would apparently intoxicate the person or increase their intoxication so that they would be in danger of causing injury to another person or property.'),
('A patron sold liquor while intoxicated later dies in an accident. Under LLCA section 52, which action may be brought?',
 'A Family Law Act claim', ['A building code complaint', 'A tax appeal', 'A Small Claims debt case'],
 'If the person dies by accident or by suicide while so intoxicated, section 52 allows an action under Part V of the Family Law Act against whoever sold the liquor.'),
('Apart from AGCO penalties, what other risk do servers and licensees face for harm caused by over-service?',
 'Civil liability', ["Loss of a driver's licence", 'Losing their health card', 'A ban on travel'],
 'The AGCO warns that beyond regulatory penalties, licensees and staff may face civil liability for conduct that causes harm, such as over-serving a patron.'),
('A licensee writes a house policy that allows serving until 2:30 a.m. Which rule applies?',
 'The law wins', ['The policy wins', 'Both apply equally', 'The server chooses'],
 "House policies are not the law and do not override obligations under the LLCA, its regulations and the Registrar's standards."),
("A bar's licence states a capacity of 120. Who counts toward that number?",
 'Patrons and staff', ['Paying patrons', 'Seated guests', 'Guests over 19'],
 'The number of people permitted on the licence includes staff and anyone working for the licensee as well as customers. Separate licensed areas cannot combine their capacities.'),
('A new General Delivery Licence holder wants to sell its own stock of liquor. What does the licence allow?',
 'Delivery only, not sales', ['Both sales and delivery', 'Sales at events only', 'Wholesale sales to bars'],
 'Delivery licences let a business deliver liquor for a fee. They do not let the holder sell liquor.'),
('At an AGCO inspection, how should staff treat the inspector?',
 'Cooperate and answer truthfully', ['Ask them to come back later', 'Answer questions only in writing', 'Let the owner do the talking'],
 'Staff should welcome the inspector, answer all questions truthfully, provide requested records and never block or interfere with the inspection.'),
('When did the Liquor Licence and Control Act, 2019 come into force?',
 'November 29, 2021', ['January 1, 2019', 'July 1, 2022', 'September 30, 2020'],
 'The LLCA came into force on November 29, 2021, replacing the Liquor Licence Act and the Liquor Control Act.'),
]
